  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-lab art direction, disciplined dark palette, vivid coral/cyan accents, and a confident headline create clear identity. Desktop hierarchy is compelling, but the atlas grid is overly dense and visibly clips/truncates card content. Tablet and mobile adapt structurally, yet become exceptionally long, with tiny mono labels, low-emphasis gray copy, and a large raw JSON block that weakens polish. The compact headers also truncate navigation and feel crowded rather than deliberately resolved.",
    "fix": "Increase small-text size and contrast, eliminate desktop card clipping, and replace or collapse the raw JSON block into a styled metadata summary. Tighten vertical rhythm on narrow screens and give the mobile/tablet header a cleaner explicit overflow treatment.",
